What was the year in which the lease on Hong Kong officially expired, as per the terms of the Sino-British Joint Declaration?
According to the context, the lease of the New Territories was set to expire according to the Convention for the Extension of Hong Kong Territory, and the Sino-British Joint Declaration was signed to stipulate the sovereign and administrative arrangement over Hong Kong after this expiration. The lease was for a period of 99 years starting from 1 July 1898. 

To find the year in which the lease officially expired, we need to add 99 years to 1898. 

1898 + 99 = 1997

Therefore, the year in which the lease on Hong Kong officially expired, as per the terms of the Sino-British Joint Declaration, is 1997.
