Which of the two houses identified in the previous steps is the lower house of the British parliament, and what are its specific roles and responsibilities within the British parliamentary system.
Based on the provided context, the lower house of the British parliament is the House of Commons. Its specific roles and responsibilities include:

*   It is an elected body consisting of 650 members known as Members of Parliament (MPs).
*   Members are elected to represent constituencies by first-past-the-post and hold their seats until the next general election.
*   The House of Commons is the more powerful house and can usually vote to overrule amendments proposed by the House of Lords.
*   Most important laws are introduced in the House of Commons, and the government schedules the vast majority of parliamentary business in this house.
