What is the history of disciplinary actions in English football leagues, specifically focusing on the introduction of red and yellow cards?
The introduction of red and yellow cards in English football leagues dates back to the 1976-77 season. This was the first time coloured cards were used in domestic English football to indicate disciplinary actions. The idea of using coloured cards originated with English referee Ken Aston, who was appointed to the FIFA Referees' Committee and was responsible for referees at the 1966 FIFA World Cup.
